====Noun====
{{sv-noun|n}}

# [[sheep]] (animal)
#: {{ux|sv|– Far, får '''får''' '''får'''? – Nej, '''får''' får inte '''får'''. '''Får''' får lamm.|– Father, do '''sheep''' have '''sheep''' [Father, get '''sheep''' '''sheep''']? – No, '''sheep''' do not have '''sheep''' [No, '''sheep''' get not '''sheep''']. '''Sheep''' have lambs ['''Sheep''' get lambs]. [well-known wordplay]}}
# [[mutton]] (as part of a dish – might get qualified as {{m|sv|fårkött}} ["sheep meat"] otherwise)
#: {{ux|sv|[[w:sv:får i kål|'''får''' i kål]]|{{w|fårikål}} ["'''mutton''' in cabbage" – a Norwegian dish]}}
#: {{ux|sv|'''får'''{{l|sv|rätter}}|'''mutton''' dishes}}
# {{lb|sv|derogatory}} a [[sheep]] (easily led person)
# {{lb|sv|chiefly|Christianity|chiefly plural}} a [[sheep]] (religious adherent – compare {{m|sv|flock}})

